      "message": "Thanks, the batch rule looks right to me now: a small folio is only freed when every slice PTE that maps it is in the batch, and native folios take the same path as before.\n\nCould this follow the MADV_COLD/MADV_PAGEOUT walk from aosp/4367604, so that the two walks stay alike? `folio_size(folio) / PAGE_SIZE` is the right count, since `mm/madvise.c` includes `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`. But `vma_folio_nr_ptes()` (aosp/4390444) already gives that count, so the `folio_nr_ptes` local wouldn\u0027t be needed.\n\nThe small-folio check could then move into a helper next to `p3s_madvise_folio_pte_batch()` in `mm/p3s/rmap.h`, with the 16KB/4KB explanation as its kernel-doc, so that `madvise_free_pte_range()` keeps a one-line hook. Something like:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool p3s_folio_slices_in_batch(const struct vm_area_struct *vma,\n\t\t\t\t\t     const struct folio *folio, int nr)\n{\n\treturn !vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) || folio_test_large(folio) ||\n\t       folio_mapcount(folio) \u003d\u003d nr;\n}\n```\n\nand in `madvise_free_pte_range()`:\n\n```\n\t\tif (folio_test_large(folio) || vma_is_p3s_4k(vma)) {\n\t\t\tnr \u003d madvise_folio_pte_batch(vma, addr, end, folio,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t     pte, \u0026ptent);\n\t\t\tif (!p3s_folio_slices_in_batch(vma, folio, nr))\n\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\tif (nr \u003c vma_folio_nr_ptes(vma, folio)) {\n```\n\nUpstream\u0027s comment above `folio_mapcount(folio) !\u003d nr` could then stay, with \"the number of PTEs in the batch\" instead of \"its number of pages\", as aosp/4367604 has it for MADV_COLD. No stub is needed, since `vma_is_p3s_4k()` is false without `CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE`.",
